  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; governmental funds only (no business-type). Trimmed pages: p1-3 government-wide statement (printed pp7-9), p4-5 governmental funds statement (printed pp10-11), p6-14 fund budget schedules (printed pp33-41). Beginning 5,066,505 is the printed beginning fund balance including a 14,920 'Change in leasing corporation' (as previously reported 5,051,585), so no adjustment; cash basis so fund balance = cash. Receipts from the funds statement total (p4) 24,823,771; 'Other local receipts' 410,244 split using General Fund schedule p6 lines (tuition 137,900 + preschool tuition 87,131 + rentals 34,213 = 259,244 = charges for services on p1; plus 151,000 corporate/private grants). Transfers 436,144 (General to Nutrition) net to zero in the total column. Hidden transfer: General Fund line 2900 Other Support Services 75,000 equals the transfer to the Depreciation Fund (the statement's General Fund column combines General and Depreciation and shows disbursements 22,145,794 = schedule 22,586,788 - 436,144 transfers + 70,150 Depreciation spending - 75,000); recorded as contra -75,000 plus other financing -75,000, flagged for review. The Depreciation Fund and General Fund are combined in the statement's General Fund column. General Fund detail kept by program line (no program-by-object exhibit in the trimmed PDF); no student per-account activities schedule, so the Activities Fund budget schedule is used. General Fund expenditure total 22,586,788 includes transfers out and the hidden transfer (includes other financing). Instruction on p4 (14,478,145) = lines 1xxx 11,169,588 + 3400/3541/3551 362,339 + 6xxx federal programs 2,946,218. Beginning fund balances on schedules differ slightly from the statement because Depreciation is combined with General. No balance sheet liabilities (cash basis); total_liabilities null. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
